+## 1. Joined rank-envelope framed DAG (agent ID7RD501bCJtnCzpz1PA6U-glaring, clearexit)
+
+- Construction: FJ joined rank-envelope as permutation-framed DAG.
+- n=3: 11 nodes, depth 3 — checker ACCEPT.
+- n=4: 47 nodes, depth 5 — checker ACCEPT.
+- n=5: 199 nodes, depth 6 — checker REJECTS (64/120 inputs reach unsorted leaf).
+- Obstruction: zero-comparison insertions attach a slot move to the preceding comparison edge; that move depends on value state before the edge, not only the outcome prefix. A shared node can require different frames in different value contexts (e.g. comparison [4,2] needs [0,1,3,4,2] vs [1,2,4,0,3]); no fixed permutation sorts both.
+- Does not establish polynomial-size completeness; n=5 is the first failure.
+- Full report: /home/lubko/soring-fronts/framed-dag-joined-rank-envelope-n7-20261121/exec-report.md.
+- Posted to #301 at 2026-11-21T04:44:40Z.
+
+## 2. Ford–Johnson/Jacobsthal framed DAG (agent x1YMHyGw9Ev7IlOXHPmTwV-mimicked, clearexit)
+
+- Result: no falsifier; standard FJ/Jacobsthal schedule admits a sound O(n^2)-node permutation-framed DAG at height F_FJ(n) (paper-argument level). Pairing O(n) nodes; recursive winner sort O(n^2); insertions O(n) each (binary search over O(n) positions); odd straggler O(n).
+- Limits: paper proof only; no generated certificate for n>6; no checker run of recursive frames; odd case not independently audited.
+- This is a soundness certificate for the FJ upper bound F_FJ(n), not completeness at exact S(n) (F_FJ(n) != S(n) for some n, e.g. ~47).
+- Posted to #301 at 2026-11-21T04:38:59Z.
+
+## 3. Rank-envelope grammar soundness (agent qCsdMQjp8ppNSqVGVKYunX-lied, clearexit)
+
+- Result: rank-envelope construction completes as sound polynomial framed DAG for FJ (linear surplus Theta(n)), but does not by itself justify Sergeev's o(n) surplus; coupled containers in group insertion force either looser windows (reverting to linear) or join-incompatible (superpolynomial) framed states.
+- Claim tested: polynomial-size sound framed DAG of height log2(n!)+o(n) via rank-envelope insertion.
+- What works: FJ pending loser anchored by paired winner; weak invariant sound; joins succeed; O(n^2) nodes at height F_FJ(n)=log2(n!)+Theta(n).
+- Obstruction for o(n): Sergeev group insertion couples pending keys through containers; endpoints depend on which container elements extracted/inserted; tracking for tight windows is exponential in container configurations.
+- Honest limit: structural obstruction for this specific weak-window construction, not a proved lower bound against all polynomial framed DAGs at log2(n!)+o(n).
+- No exec-report.md was written by the agent; full argument in agent log.
+- Posted to #301 at 2026-11-21T04:44:48Z.
+
+## Open obligations preserved
